Sort List Of Lists
==================

Write a function:

    def sort_list_of_lists(lst: list[list[int]]) -> list[list[int]]

Given a list of integer lists, return a new list where every inner list is
sorted in ascending order. The order of the outer list stays the same.

Examples:
    sort_list_of_lists([[3, 1, 2], [6, 5, 4], [9, 8, 7]]) -> [[1, 2, 3], [4, 5, 6], [7, 8, 9]]
    sort_list_of_lists([[10, 9], [8, 7], [6, 5]]) -> [[9, 10], [7, 8], [5, 6]]
    sort_list_of_lists([[1], [3, 2], [5, 4, 6]]) -> [[1], [2, 3], [4, 5, 6]]
    sort_list_of_lists([]) -> []
